, "summary": "thinking (17 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "65319851-5e04-5899-90ef-aa9315334fb5", "at": 1795626449.8563137, "until": 1795626451.2118566, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3179, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "12b421b6b444c7bd16ef948d74c9634f", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01Q9pBL6QvdB7KDL8SMmJKXw", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian && rm -rf idea-wiki && git clone -q $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git idea-wiki && cd idea-wiki && git log --oneline|head -2; grep -n -iE \"CPU-h|cut order|never cut|total\" Brief.md", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian && rm -rf idea-wiki && git clone -q $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git idea-wiki && cd idea-wiki && git log --oneline|head -2; grep -n -iE \"CPU-h|cut order|never cut|total\" Brief.md"]], "output": "```console\n33414bf Brief rev 3: fraction-based low-d budgets, cost table re-based, tolerance and statistics caveats\n076e706 Brief rev 2: definitions, reference classes, compute table and ranking after idea review 1\n36:- H4 Within-run variance + *estimated* margin predicts instability. Exact margin is used only for H2 diagnostics; the certificate uses only run-available quantities, and the selection bias of a margin computed from the same noisy φ is analysed. First validate the variance estimator (unbiased Kernel SHAP / bootstrap over coalitions) for coverage. Compare: (i) one run at budget 2m + variance check versus (ii) two runs at m + agreement, at equal total budget; report calibration (reliability curve, Brier) not only AUROC, and budget saved by the minimum-budget rule versus a flat larger budget. Validation: held-out instances/models within dataset as the main split; leave-one-dataset-out with N stated as small.\n46:| 1 grid | d ≥ 16 datasets: m ∈ {256, 1024, 2d+2048, 4096}, n ≈ 60 instances, R = 60 (R = 100 for headline cells); d ≤ 10: m ∈ {5%, 15%, 50%} of the 2^d−2 non-trivial coalitions (Pima 13/38/127; d=10: 51/153/511 — sampled for every d), plus the shap default (exact for these d), n ≈ 100, R = 100 | d ≥ 16: ≈ 1.4 s per RF stream of 4096×50 ⇒ 3.6k runs ≈ 1.4 CPU-h per RF cell **per estimator stream** (default Kernel SHAP, paired/unbiased, permutation ⇒ ×3, partly offset by cheaper LR/MLP and by cache reuse), so ~10–12 CPU-h per d ≥ 16 dataset before re-timing, not 4–5; d ≤ 10: ≈ 0.2 s per run ⇒ ~2–3 CPU-h per dataset over all models and estimators |\n47:| 1 references + floors | E1/E2/E3 per above; retrain floor with 10 models on a subset of instances | ≈ 5–6 CPU-h for E1/E2 and the floors of RF/GBM/LR; plus German MLP E1 (≈ 5·10^7 evals ≈ 2.5 min per instance × a reduced set of ~30 instances ≈ 1.3 CPU-h) and, for MLPs at d=20, floor (c) with an E3-flagged reference (MLP retrains × high-budget runs; ≈ 1–2 CPU-h) |\n48:| Total tier 1 | | **≈ 30–40 CPU-h at current estimates, over the ~24 h envelope**; so the grid is cut by the order below to fit after re-timing, and the paper states what was cut |\n51:Cut order if compute falls short: tier 2 → R and n on non-headline cells → permutation estimator on d ≥ 16 datasets → low-d datasets down to Pima + one of Income/GMSC → paired/unbiased stream limited to the cells where the certificate (H4) is tested. The German Credit and ACS-Employment cells with RF/GBM/MLP are never cut. Execution, caching, parallelism and exact timings belong to `experiment-repo`.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "524278aa-1ce2-562b-ab8d-9dd2df8504c2", "at": 1795626449.9334629, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 3181, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "12b421b6b444c7bd16ef948d74c9634f", "trust": "a